{"name":"Cool Vapour","hex":"#d5d7d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a mildly low temperature.","Allowing or suggesting heat relief."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A moderate or refreshing state of cold; moderate temperature of the air between hot and cold; coolness.","A calm temperament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool"},{"term":"vapour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vapour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vapor","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, a vapor or vapour is a substance in the gas phase at a temperature lower than its critical temperature, which means that the vapor can be condensed to a liquid by increasing the pressure on it without reducing the temperature of the vapor. A vapor is different from an aerosol. An aerosol is a suspension of tiny particles of liquid, solid, or both within a gas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg/330px-Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vapor","wikidata":"Q255722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/500px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/1280px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/500px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par